{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSZY5X9TZodMZMMp3ZCV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The rule keeps only what each sub-property needs:\n\n- **Units: keep.** A cut unit is never refined, so a wrong cut leaves the sub-property unproved for good. For example, a cut CSR file could raise unconstrained interrupts, and a cut icache could raise unconstrained fetch exceptions. Proving the sub-property matters more than its size.\n- **Operators: keep.** A 32-bit adder is cheap for the solver, and \"uf\" saves almost no state bits. A spurious \"uf\" counterexample could also make refinement restore a havoced register first.\n- **Registers kept:**\n  - The register of every compared state `xk`. Its start assumption and recorder assumption are needed for the comparison.\n  - Every register that the case fixes through an operand field (`rs1==j`, `rs2==j`).\n  - x0 whenever a read register is x0, so that the ILA's x0 reads as zero.\n- **Unknown read registers.** If an operand field is not fixed by the case and the compared states may depend on it, all registers are kept. This covers JALR's pc and unknown states. The ADDI \"mem\" sub-property compares only pc, load_en, store_en and x0, which do not depend on the source registers. There, every other register is havoced.\n- **All other registers: havoc.** This gives the smallest cone, and it is safe because the proof does not read them.\n\n```python\ndef instr_name(design):\n    desc = design.get(\"description\", \"\") or \"\"\n    lines = desc.split(\"\\n\")\n    first = lines[0] if lines else \"\"\n    toks = [t.strip() for t in first.split()]\n    for i, t in enumerate(toks):\n        if t == \"/\" and i + 1 < len(toks):\n            return toks[i + 1].strip().strip(\".\").upper()\n    return \"\"\n\n\ndef gpr_of_state(s):\n    if len(s) >= 2 and s[0] == \"x\" and s[1:].isdigit():\n        return int(s[1:])\n    return None\n\n\ndef choose(sub, design):\n    choices = design.get(\"choices\", [])\n    states = sub.get(\"states\", []) or []\n    terms = sub.get(\"case_terms\", []) or []\n    operand_fields = design.get(\"operand_fields\", []) or []\n\n    keep_regs = set()\n    keep_all = False\n\n    # registers of compared states\n    for s in states:\n        r = gpr_of_state(s)\n        if r is not None:\n            keep_regs.add(r)\n\n    # operand registers fixed by the case\n    fixed_fields = set()\n    for t in terms:\n        f = t.get(\"field\")\n        if f in (\"rs1\", \"rs2\") and t.get(\"op\") == \"==\":\n            fixed_fields.add(f)\n            try:\n                keep_regs.add(int(t.get(\"value\")))\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n        elif f in operand_fields and t.get(\"op\") == \"==\":\n            fixed_fields.add(f)\n            try:\n                keep_regs.add(int(t.get(\"value\")))\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n\n    # operand fields not fixed by the case: may the compared states depend on them?\n    unfixed = [f for f in operand_fields if f not in fixed_fields]\n    if len(unfixed) > 0:\n        safe_states = set([\"pc\", \"load_en\", \"store_en\", \"x0\"])\n        has_gpr_state = any(\n            gpr_of_state(s) is not None and gpr_of_state(s) != 0 for s in states\n        )\n        name = instr_name(design)\n        only_safe = all(s in safe_states for s in states)\n        if has_gpr_state or (not only_safe) or name in (\"JALR\",):\n            keep_all = True\n\n    # x0 needed whenever a read register is x0 (ILA x0 == 0 assumption)\n    if 0 in keep_regs:\n        keep_regs.add(0)\n\n    result = {}\n    for c in choices:\n        cid = c[\"id\"]\n        kind = c.get(\"kind\")\n        levels = c.get(\"levels\", [])\n        if kind == \"unit\":\n            lvl = \"keep\"\n        elif kind == \"operator\":\n            lvl = \"keep\"\n        elif kind == \"gpr\":\n            r = c.get(\"register\")\n            try:\n                r = int(r)\n            except Exception:\n                r = -1\n            if keep_all or r in keep_regs:\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n            else:\n                lvl = \"havoc\"\n        else:\n            lvl = \"keep\"\n        if lvl not in levels:\n            lvl = \"keep\" if \"keep\" in levels else levels[0]\n        result[cid] = lvl\n    return result\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24945,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24945},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21eb92a6-e27b-4fc6-9498-493481766061","uuid":"6de0022c-582a-4257-a53a-b2ae047e5d75","timestamp":"2026-10-27T10:12:18.925Z","request_id":"req_011CgSZY5JjkCjBZNxKqfiZe"}
